Stack: SDD

Purpose:
  The .sdd system's technology selection and stack information layer.
   This directory defines technology constraints, compatibility rules,
   and selection mechanisms. Project-specific selected stack is stored
   in .sdd/instances/vkard.az/stack/. Separation: root = reusable technology
   constraints, project = concrete selection.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1  @languages.sdd
   2  @backend.sdd
   3  @frontend.sdd
   4  @mobile.sdd
   5  @database.sdd
   6  @cache.sdd
   7  @messaging.sdd
   8  @testing.sdd
   9  @infrastructure.sdd
   10  @observability.sdd

Modes:
  ANALYZE   — technology selection and fit analysis
  PLAN      — stack decision and technology mapping
  WORK      — technology-based implementation
  VERIFY    — stack compliance check
  REVIEW    — technology decision execution

Rules:
  [STK1]  Technology selection MUST follow architecture, not precede it.
  [STK2]  AI MUST NOT hard-code universal technology preferences — all
          scores are decision aids, not mandates.
  [STK3]  Technology decisions MUST be recorded with rationale and
          alternatives considered.
  [STK4]  Stack compatibility (BE + FE + MD + DB + Cache + Messaging +
          Testing + Security + DevOps + Observability) MUST be validated
          before finalizing selection.
  [STK5]  Version policies MUST be recorded as current stable / current
          supported / LTS, never as hard-coded versions.
  [STK6]  AI MUST NOT modify stack knowledge without TECH_UPDATE_PROPOSAL
          and human approval.
  [STK7]  Cross-layer impact MUST be analyzed when stack changes.
  [STK8]  Breaking changes in API contracts MUST trigger FE/MD/API test
          task creation.
  [STK9]  Contextual skill loading MUST be based on task impact, not
          loading all stack skills for every task.
  [STK10] Project stack MUST be traceable to architecture decisions and
          project requirements.

Entry:
  Read:
    INDEX.sdd

  Resolve:
    languages
    backend
    frontend
    mobile
    database
    cache
    messaging
    testing
    infrastructure
    observability

Navigation:
  Stack: @stack/INDEX.sdd
  Languages: @stack/languages.sdd
  Backend: @stack/backend.sdd
  Frontend: @stack/frontend.sdd
  Mobile: @stack/mobile.sdd
  Database: @stack/database.sdd
  Cache: @stack/cache.sdd
  Messaging: @stack/messaging.sdd
  Testing: @stack/testing.sdd
  Infrastructure: @stack/infrastructure.sdd
  Observability: @stack/observability.sdd
  ProjectStack: @instances/vkard.az/stack/INDEX.sdd

State: +
  Note:
  Stack directory created as the technology
  selection and knowledge layer. Root stack/ defines reusable technology
  constraints and compatibility rules; instances/vkard.az/stack/ stores the selected
  technology instances for the current project. Separation follows
  ROOT-001: root = reusable system intelligence, project = concrete
  project state.
